# Vendored third-party sources are kept byte-identical to upstream.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this repository's usual Windows checkout, which would
# rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout and break the sha256 recorded in each vendored
# README. These paths are declared binary so Git never touches a byte of them.
#
# The licence-header CI job skips third_party/ for the same reason: these files
# carry their own upstream SPDX identifiers, not ours.
third_party/tweetnacl/tweetnacl.c -text
third_party/tweetnacl/tweetnacl.h -text
